Agent: You decided to use acrylic paint for your canvas hobby project.

Quick reminder + next steps:
- Why acrylic: fast-drying, versatile, easy clean-up, layers well on canvas.
- Recommended supplies:
  - Acrylic paints (student or professional—brands: Liquitex, Golden, Winsor & Newton)
  - Pre-primed canvas or gesso to prime raw canvas
  - Synthetic brushes (flats, rounds) and a palette knife
  - Palette (plastic or stay-wet) and a spray bottle to slow drying
  - Acrylic mediums (gloss/matte medium, retarder if you want more open time)
  - Acrylic varnish for final protection
  - Rags, jar for water, and a non-absorbent surface to mix on
- Quick tips:
  - Work in layers; thin with medium or water (don’t over-thin).
  - Use a retarder or keep a mist bottle if you need more blending time.
  - Let each layer dry before glazing or varnishing.
  - Clean brushes promptly with soap and water.

Want me to:
- Create a shopping list/draft email to order these supplies?
- Search your emails/drafts for any earlier shopping notes or specific paint brand you mentioned?
